course: dictionary
lesson: 4288
title: Greet and greetings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To greet someone means to say hello or welcome them when you meet. You can greet people with words, a smile, a wave, a handshake or a hug. The noun is greeting, as in «a friendly greeting».
explain: Greet can also mean to react to something in a certain way. «The news was greeted with cheers» means people cheered when they heard it. Look at the words around greet to find its meaning.
explain: «A girl in Leeds would not greet or answer her new teacher for weeks» was not being rude. The sentence goes on: she was shy, and the teacher thought she was unhappy. Clues like this show you what a word means in the story.
explain: Greetings change from place to place. A hongi, a namaste with palms pressed together, and a simple wave are all ways of greeting. Good manners mean saying hello, looking at the person and smiling.
fact: Greet is a verb; the noun is greeting.
fact: «Greet» means to say hello or welcome someone when you meet them.
fact: You can greet someone with words, a smile, a wave, a handshake, a bow or a hug.
fact: «The hongi is a traditional Maori greeting in New Zealand, done when you are invited.»
fact: «Namaste» with palms pressed together is a respectful Indian and Nepali greeting.
exercise: «Many families greet in their own way.» What does greet mean here? | *To say hello or welcome someone | To sing a loud song | To run away from someone | To cook a meal for someone
exercise: «The news was greeted with cheers.» What does greeted mean here? | Said goodbye to | Hid from | *Reacted to, in a certain way, such as cheering | Wrote down
exercise: Which is NOT a way to greet someone? | A handshake | A hug | A wave | *A loud slam of the door
test: In «A girl in Leeds would not greet or answer her new teacher for weeks», what was the real reason? | She was rude | *She was shy | She had lost her bag | She did not like school lunch
test: Which greeting has palms pressed together? | A hongi | A handshake | *Namaste | A wave
exam: Why does the way a character greets someone show whether they are friendly? | Because greet means to shout | *Because how a character greets someone shows how they feel | Because greeting always takes a long time | Because greetings are only for birthdays
